  "chapter": 575,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 29 Chapter 575\n\n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 3012, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  insurance law, in relation to revising the\n        standards relating to the board of directors  of  domestic  life\n        insurance companies\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  This bill would exempt certain domestic stock life insurance organiza-\ntions  from  having at least one-third of their directors be independent\n-- meaning one-third of the directors cannot be officers or employees of\nthe organization. Having independent directors with  no  affiliation  to\nthe  organization  allows for more stringent oversight and monitoring of\nthe organization's activities.\n\n  My administration has made significant efforts  to  limit  unnecessary\nregulations  and  requirements on businesses in New York State. However,\nthis bill would limit the amount of  independent  oversight  and  review\nconducted  by  the  Boards of Directors of such organizations, including\nless oversight of investment transactions.\n\n  Having independent directors is essential for protecting the interests\nof policyholders and residents of the State. The Legislature has  agreed\nto  a  chapter  amendment to address these concerns. On that basis, I am\nsigning this bill.\n\n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2015
 },
